    <p>Sellers also buy "GDPR-compliant" templates as digital downloads, often on Etsy itself. They can work, but they are still static text. Whatever you start from, check it against the list in the previous sections and remove anything that does not describe your shop.</p>

    <h2 id="generator">Using BuildPrivacyPolicy's Generator for Etsy Sellers</h2>

    <p>The generator is built for apps and websites, so a few answers need translating for an Etsy shop. You can <a href="https://buildprivacypolicy.com/">create your Etsy shop's policy with the generator</a> using these settings:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>App name and contact email:</strong> your shop name and the email you want privacy requests sent to.</li>
      <li><strong>Platforms:</strong> select <em>Web App / PWA</em>, since buyers reach your shop through the web.</li>
      <li><strong>App profile:</strong> choose <em>E-commerce / subscription</em> to prefill sensible commerce answers.</li>
      <li><strong>Regions:</strong> pick where your buyers are, for example <em>United States</em>, <em>EU / UK / Switzerland</em> and <em>Canada</em>, or <em>Worldwide</em> if you ship everywhere.</li>
      <li><strong>Data collected:</strong> <em>Name</em>, <em>Email</em>, <em>Address</em>, <em>Purchases</em> and <em>Messages/chat</em>; add <em>Photos/videos</em> if buyers send reference images for custom work. Leave <em>Payment info</em> unselected, because Etsy handles payments.</li>
      <li><strong>Recipients:</strong> <em>Payment processor</em> for Etsy Payments, plus <em>Messaging</em>, <em>Analytics</em> or <em>Other</em> for your email tool, shipping software or print partner.</li>
      <li><strong>Retention and requests:</strong> <em>Legal/business need</em> for order records, and <em>Privacy email</em> as the way buyers contact you.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>When you generate, you get a hosted URL you can link from anywhere, plus HTML and plain-text downloads; copy the text into the Privacy tab in Shop Manager. There is no account, no email verification and no payment. The output is structured around the GDPR, CCPA and the other regions you select. It is not legal advice, and a shop selling to children or handling health-related custom orders should have it reviewed.</p>

    <h2 id="example-policy">Sample Etsy Shop Privacy Policy You Can Copy</h2>

    <p>Below is a complete privacy policy for a fictional Etsy shop called "[Your Shop Name]." It covers the default Etsy data flows (order details from Etsy, Etsy Payments, Etsy Messages, Etsy Ads and Offsite Ads) and the most common outside tools. Copy the whole block, replace the bracketed placeholders, and delete any section that does not apply to your shop.</p>

    <div class="copy-block">
      <div class="copy-block-header">
        <span class="copy-block-label">Sample Privacy Policy — ready to copy</span>
      </div>
      <div class="copy-block-body" id="sample-policy-text">
<p><strong>Privacy Policy for [Your Shop Name]</strong></p>
<p><em>Last updated: [Date]</em></p>

<p><strong>1. Who I Am</strong></p>
<p>[Your Shop Name] is run by [your name or business name], [business address if you are a registered trader] ("I," "me," or "my"). I sell through my Etsy shop at [your-shop-url]. For personal data I receive as a seller, I am the data controller. This policy covers only the data I handle as a seller. Etsy has its own privacy policy that governs how the Etsy platform collects and uses data.</p>

<p><strong>2. Data I Collect</strong></p>
<p><em>Order data.</em> When you place an order, Etsy provides me with your name, shipping address, the items you ordered, the price paid, and any personalization or gift message you add. Etsy may also show me your email address on the order.</p>
<p><em>Messages.</em> If you contact me through Etsy Messages, I receive the content of your messages, your Etsy username, and any photos or files you attach.</p>
<p><em>Payment information.</em> Payments are processed by Etsy through Etsy Payments. I never receive or store your card number, bank details or other payment credentials.</p>
<p>[If applicable:] <em>Newsletter.</em> If you sign up for my newsletter on [where], I collect your email address and the date you subscribed.</p>

<p><strong>3. How I Use Your Data and Why</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>To make, ship and deliver your order and to send order updates (necessary to perform our contract)</li>
<li>To answer your messages and handle returns or problems with an order (necessary to perform our contract)</li>
<li>To keep order records for tax and accounting (legal obligation)</li>
<li>[If applicable:] To send marketing emails, only if you have opted in (consent, which you can withdraw at any time)</li>
</ul>
<p>I do not add buyers to any mailing list without their consent, and I do not sell your personal data.</p>

<p><strong>4. Who Receives Your Data</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Etsy, Inc.</strong> hosts my shop, processes payments through Etsy Payments, provides Etsy Messages, and handles cases and disputes, under Etsy's own privacy policy.</li>
<li><strong>Shipping carriers.</strong> [USPS / UPS / FedEx / Royal Mail / Canada Post] receive your name and address to deliver your order. [If applicable:] I create labels with [Etsy shipping labels / Pirate Ship / ShipStation / Shippo], which also processes your name and address.</li>
<li>[If applicable:] <strong>[Printful / Printify / Gelato / your supplier].</strong> Produces and ships some items, and receives your name, address and order details to do so.</li>
<li>[If applicable:] <strong>[Mailchimp / Klaviyo / Flodesk].</strong> Stores newsletter subscribers' email addresses and sends my emails.</li>
<li>[If applicable:] <strong>[QuickBooks / Wave / Craftybase].</strong> Receives order totals, dates and basic buyer details for bookkeeping.</li>
</ul>
<p>I do not share your personal data with anyone else unless the law requires it.</p>

<p><strong>5. Advertising</strong></p>
<p>[If applicable:] I use Etsy Ads to promote my listings within Etsy. Etsy may also advertise my listings on other sites, such as Google, Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest and Bing, through its Offsite Ads program. Etsy runs these ads and any related tracking under its own privacy policy. I do not receive information about who sees or clicks them.</p>

<p><strong>6. International Transfers</strong></p>
<p>[If you are in the EU or UK and use non-EU services:] Some of the services above are based outside [the EU / the UK], including in the United States. Where data is transferred, it is protected by [the EU-US Data Privacy Framework / standard contractual clauses / the UK International Data Transfer Addendum].</p>

<p><strong>7. How Long I Keep Data</strong></p>
<p>Order records are kept for [6] years to meet tax and accounting rules. Messages stay in Etsy Messages for as long as my shop is open. [If applicable:] Newsletter data is kept until you unsubscribe and is removed from my list within [7] days. After that, data is deleted or anonymized.</p>

<p><strong>8. Your Rights</strong></p>
<p>If you are in the EU, EEA or UK, you can ask me to access, correct or delete the personal data I hold about you, to restrict or object to its use, or to give you a copy in a portable format, and you can withdraw consent at any time. You can also complain to your local data protection authority. If you live in a US state with a consumer privacy law, you may have similar rights to know about and delete your data. For data Etsy holds, contact Etsy through its Help Center. For data I hold, email me at [your-email@example.com]. I will reply within one month.</p>

<p><strong>9. Security</strong></p>
<p>Etsy encrypts traffic on its platform and secures payments. I protect my Etsy account and any tools I use with strong passwords and two-factor authentication, and I only keep printed shipping details as long as I need them to send your order.</p>

<p><strong>10. Changes to This Policy</strong></p>
<p>If I change this policy, I will update the "Last updated" date above.</p>

<p><strong>11. Contact</strong></p>
<p>Questions about this policy or your data:<br />[your-email@example.com]<br />[Your Shop Name], [business address if required]</p>
      </div>
