    <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Does Etsy provide a privacy policy for sellers?</h3>
        <p>Etsy offers a sample privacy policy in the Privacy tab of your shop policies (Shop Manager, then Settings, then Policy settings) that you can customize. It is a generic starting point: it does not name the shipping, email, print-on-demand or bookkeeping tools you use, so you still need to edit it, or replace it with a policy generated from your own setup. Etsy's own privacy policy covers only Etsy's processing, not yours.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do I need a privacy policy for my Etsy shop?</h3>
        <p>If you are based in the EU or offer items to buyers in the EU, yes: Etsy requires you to create and comply with a GDPR-compliant privacy policy. For other sellers Etsy recommends one, and laws in many places, including the UK, Canada and some US states, can require it depending on where your buyers are and how much data you handle.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What privacy laws apply to Etsy sellers?</h3>
        <p>That depends on where your buyers are, not only where you are. EU buyers bring in the GDPR, UK buyers the UK GDPR, Canadian buyers PIPEDA and Brazilian buyers the LGPD. US state laws such as the CCPA apply only to businesses above their revenue or data thresholds. Etsy's Seller Policy also treats you as an independent controller of buyer data under EU law.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Where do I put my privacy policy on Etsy?</h3>
        <p>On Etsy.com, open Shop Manager, go to Settings, then Policy settings, and open the Privacy tab. Select Create a policy (or edit your existing one), paste your text or customize Etsy's sample, and select Publish. Shop policies cannot be edited in the Etsy Seller app, so use a desktop or mobile browser.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Can I add Etsy buyers to my email list?</h3>
        <p>Not without their consent. Etsy's Seller Policy says you may not add any Etsy member to an email or physical mailing list without consent, and Etsy advises never copying email addresses from orders into a list. EU and UK rules also require express consent for marketing emails. Use an opt-in signup form and name your email tool in your privacy policy.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do I need to disclose Etsy Ads and Offsite Ads in my privacy policy?</h3>
        <p>A short note is good practice. Etsy runs Etsy Ads and Offsite Ads, and the related tracking, under its own privacy policy, and you receive no data about who sees or clicks an ad, so the note can point buyers to Etsy's policy. Offsite Ads run on Google, Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, Bing and Etsy partner sites; shops that reach $10,000 in sales in any 365-day period cannot opt out.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Should I buy a GDPR-compliant privacy policy template for my Etsy shop?</h3>
